{
 "result": "csvsum.py is a split-based reader: it reads stdin as bytes, normalises CR/LF, splits on commas, groups the val tokens by cat in a dict, and sums each group with fsum before printing sorted \"cat,sum\" lines at 2 decimals. It passes sample in-0 byte-for-byte against out-0, and assay registered a baseline of 1.76322 (noise 2.7%). I stopped here rather than spend more energy on a rewrite: the remaining obvious speedups (summing in integer cents, or plain sum() instead of fsum) risk last-digit rounding errors the harness would reject, and a win must beat the baseline by more than 3% to earn anything.",
